Subject: [PATCH 4/4] reasons: record the successor a propagated reason fired through

APPLIES ON TOP OF 0003-concrete-return-reason.patch. Three files:

  es/EscapeReasons           Via(method, ObjectNode), and per-component pointer groups.
  resolver/ReworkedResolver  collectReasons records the successor on every propagated firing;
                             stampComponent stores them once per component.
  main/Main                  printReasons writes a GROUP column and <dirname>.via.

WHY
---
TRANSITIVE_SUCCESSOR and PARAM_ESCAPES_VIA_SUCCESSOR are not causes. Each means "a successor
already escapes", and the cause is whatever made that successor escape. Counting them as
reasons double-counts: one cause is counted on the object where it fired and again, as
TRANSITIVE_SUCCESSOR, on every object upstream of it. It also names no fix, yet on
avrora (application objects, MarkStoreEscaping=false, patch 0003) TRANSITIVE_SUCCESSOR is the
second-largest single-reason bucket, 504 objects.

They cannot simply be dropped. For those 504 objects it is the only reason recorded, and
removing it would break the invariant that Escape implies a non-empty reason set. They must be
REPLACED by the causes they point to, and the enum alone cannot say where it points.

WHY RECORD THE POINTER HERE AND NOT REBUILD IT FROM .info
--------------------------------------------------------
At collectReasons the successor `nxt` is in hand at the moment the reason fires. The .info
dependency edge is not a reliable substitute: on avrora 7,726 of 18,571 internal objects
carrying TRANSITIVE_SUCCESSOR (41.6 %) have no out-edge at all (tools/orphan_transitive.py),
because purge() deletes the conditional value, and the edge with it, once an object escapes.

WHAT IS RECORDED
----------------
  * TRANSITIVE_SUCCESSOR: every successor for which isEscapingObject(nxt) held, after the same
    isReturnedFromDifferentFunction skip resolve() applies.
  * PARAM_ESCAPES_VIA_SUCCESSOR: isEscapingParam() is still what decides the reason. When it
    fires, the same loop (skip isReturnObject, test isEscapingObject) is re-run to name every
    successor it would have accepted, since isEscapingParam stops at the first.
  * The pointers are stamped component-wide, like the reasons, but stored ONCE per component
    as a group; each member holds only the group index. A pointer to a member of the same
    component is dropped, since the component already carries that member's causes.

  The first version copied the pointer union onto every member. avrora died with
  OutOfMemoryError in printReasons: the JDK half has components large enough that
  |component| x |pointers| strings do not fit in 10 GB. The verdict was unaffected (.res
  written, 0 multiset diffs); only the reason output was lost.

OUTPUT
------
  .reasons  gains a fifth column GROUP: an integer, or empty when no pointer was recorded.
            Columns 1-4 are byte-identical to patch 0003's.
  .via      new, one line per group:  <group> TAB <method>|<bci>|<objectType>;...
            The pointer field is EMPTY for a group whose propagated reason fired only inside
            its own component. Groups are numbered by first appearance in the sorted .reasons,
            so both files are deterministic. `|` and `;` cannot occur in a Soot signature.

The extractor (extract/info_to_graph.py, read_reasons mode "roots") follows object -> group ->
successor over the SCC condensation and replaces the two propagated reasons with the union of
NEAREST causes: each chain stops at the first object with a cause of its own (following every
pointer to the end merged large components into one blob; Micro-Corpus-Log F13.3). A chain
that cannot be followed becomes one of three
synthetic constants, SUCCESSOR_UNRECORDED / SUCCESSOR_NOT_IN_REASONS / SUCCESSOR_WITHOUT_CAUSE,
counted with the surrender reasons, so the invariant still holds.

WHAT IT DOES NOT CHANGE
-----------------------
No EscapeStatus is read beyond what collectReasons already read; nothing is written except the
append-only side maps, which the analysis never reads. The check is tools/verify_patch4.sh:
the .res line multiset and .reasons columns 1-4 must be identical to patch 0003's on every
corpus program.

MEASURED (Micro-Corpus-Log Phase 13)
------------------------------------
  corpus, 13 programs: .res 0 diffs, .reasons columns 1-4 0 diffs.
  avrora whole run: .res 0 diffs, columns 1-4 0 diffs, 48,097 groups.
  avrora application objects: TRANSITIVE_SUCCESSOR single-reason 504 -> 0; of 2,792 objects
  with a propagated and a direct reason, 1,598 resolve to exactly their direct reasons.
  Remaining gap: every SUCCESSOR_WITHOUT_CAUSE (17,551 objects) is in ONE resolver component of
  7,994 methods -- component-wide stamping (X-A4), not this patch.

